  "cues": [
   [
    0.104,
    "In the last lesson, electrons fell down the electron transport chain, from carrier to carrier, and ended on oxygen."
   ],
   [
    7.539,
    "The chain does something else along the way."
   ],
   [
    9.688,
    "Complexes one, three, and four use the energy of the falling electrons to pump H plus, protons, out of the matrix, and into the intermembrane space."
   ],
   [
    20.56,
    "So protons crowd in the narrow space on one side, and few remain in the matrix."
   ],
   [
    26.276,
    "That is an H plus gradient, a store of energy, like the water behind the dam."
   ],
   [
    31.615,
    "The membrane is the wall."
   ],
   [
    33.398,
    "Protons cannot simply cross it."
   ],
   [
    35.443,
    "The only open door is a protein called A T P synthase."
   ]
  ]
 },
